        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): trigger model fallback on usage-limit promptError (#103734)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen a Codex-backed turn hits the subscription usage limit, the Codex harness\nreturns a `promptError` in the attempt result instead of throwing. The host's\nmodel fallback is throw-driven — it only engages when `FailoverError` is thrown.\n\nThe existing prompt-error handler in `run.ts` already classifies the error and\nreaches `resolveRunFailoverDecision`.  However `shouldRotatePrompt` always\nreturns true for rate / billing limits, so the decision first tries **auth\nprofile rotation** — retrying the same harness with a different profile.  For\nharness-owned transports (Codex) the limit is on the harness session, not the\nprofile, so every rotation fails identically.  This wastes the user's quota\nand burns retry budget before fallback can engage.\n\nFixes #103734.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nOne targeted 8-line addition in `shouldRotatePrompt` (`failover-policy.ts`):\nwhen a plugin harness owns the transport **and** the failover reason is\n`rate_limit` or `billing`, skip profile rotation.  The decision falls through\nto `fallback_model` in `resolveRunFailoverDecision`, which throws a\n`FailoverError` that the outer fallback loop catches immediately.\n\nThis replaces the prior approach (unreachable incomplete-turn-gate\nclassification + redundant metadata classifier) with a single policy change\nat the reachable prompt-error decision boundary.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** Codex usage limit → profile rotation → all profiles fail →\nmodel fallback eventually engages (after wasted retries that consume quota).\n\n**After:** Codex usage limit → `rate_limit` failover → skips rotation →\nfalls back to next configured model (e.g. `anthropic/claude-opus-4-8`)\nimmediately.\n\nNon-harness providers and non-limit errors are unchanged — they still rotate\nprofiles before falling back.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBranch: `fix/103734-codex-usage-limit-fallback` | Base: `upstream/main`\n\n### E2E proof script\n\n```\n$ node --import tsx scripts/proof/codex-usage-limit-fallback.mts\n\n=== #103734 failover decision proof ===\n\nStep 1 — classify usage-limit → rate_limit: PASS\nStep 2 — harness-owned rate_limit → fallback_model: PASS\nStep 3 — harness-owned billing → fallback_model: PASS\nStep 4 — harness-owned server_error → rotate_profile: PASS\nStep 5 — non-harness rate_limit → rotate_profile: PASS\n\nOVERALL: ALL PASSED\n```\n\n### Failover policy tests\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/failover-policy.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  42 passed (42)\n```\n\nThree new tests:\n- harness-owned `rate_limit` prompt → `fallback_model` (skip rotation)\n- harness-owned `billing` prompt → `fallback_model` (skip rotation)\n- harness-owned `server_error` prompt → `rotate_profile` (still rotates)\n\n### Broader failover test suite\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs \\\n    src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/failover-policy.test.ts \\\n    src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/failover-observation.test.ts \\\n    src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/assistant-failover.test.ts \\\n    src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run.codex-server-error-fallback.test.ts\n\n Test Files  4 passed (4)\n      Tests  81 passed (81)\n```\n\n### Model-fallback E2E\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/model-fallback.run-embedded.e2e.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  21 passed (21)\n```\n\n### Pre-submit checks\n\n```\noxfmt --check → All matched files use the correct format\ngit diff --check → clean\n```\n\n### Diff summary\n\n```\nsrc/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/failover-policy.ts       | 11 +++++\nsrc/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/failover-policy.test.ts  | 58 ++++++++++++++\nscripts/proof/codex-usage-limit-fallback.mts                   | 102 ++++++++++++++++++++++++\n3 files changed, 171 insertions(+)\n```\n\n- [x] I understand what the code does\n- [x] Change is focused and does not mix unrelated concerns\n",
        "branch": "fix/103734-codex-usage-limit-fallback",
